#!/usr/bin/env bash
# License: GPLv3
# Credits: Felipe Facundes
# This script automates backups for Godot projects and provides restore functionality

: <<'DOCUMENTATION'
This script is designed to automate the backup process for Godot projects, ensuring that users can 
easily manage their project files and avoid accidental data loss.

Key Features:
1. Automatic Backup Creation: Creates timestamped backups of Godot projects in ~/.cache/scriptname/
2. Restore Functionality: Allows restoring projects from selected backups using dialog/whiptail
3. Signal Handling: Properly manages process termination signals
4. Size Management: Monitors backup directory size and auto-deletes oldest backups when limit reached
5. Bilingual Support: Automatically detects system language (Portuguese/English) for user messages
6. Godot Binary Selection: Can use latest binary in ~/.local/bin or specify a permanent version
7. First-run Setup: Uses zenity to select the projects directory on first execution
8. Cache Directory Management: Stores backups in ~/.cache/scriptname/ with configurable size limit
9. Project Directory Selection: Use --project to temporarily override the projects directory

DOCUMENTATION

# Define signal handler
trap 'kill $(jobs -p)' SIGTERM

